  "_source": "Hand-verified directly against RCA-DFC-REG-002.md's real per-field bit tables (0x2400-0x2438), cited by contract ID below -- same disclosed scope/rationale as every prior field-map file's own _source note (extract_registers.py does not currently preserve per-field bit ranges project-wide). RTL011_EVT_OVERFLOW_STATUS's status_registers entry below (EVENT_OVERFLOW/DROP_COUNT mapped to the generic status_o.event_overflow/event_drop_count fields dfc_rtl011_status_t carries) closes the readback gap from the start, same discipline rtl006/007/008/009/010_field_map.json established (OPEN_ISSUES.md item 21). HEALTH_STICKY's three W1C fields (ASSERTED/RECOVERED/QUALIFICATION_FAILURE) each appear in BOTH control_registers (their real clear-request fields) AND status_registers (their real sticky-readback fields), same dual-appearance pattern already used for every prior module's own multi-field W1C status registers (e.g. RTL-006's GPIO_EVENT_STATUS). dfc_rtl011_control_t grew 121->122 bits this session (approved before implementation) to add rtl011_evt_overflow_status__event_overflow at the new highest bit (121), closing the tenth real instance of the EVENT_OVERFLOW-clear-field gap class (items 2/7/8/12/20/24/28/32/36). Confirmed directly against dfc_registers_pkg.json: HEALTH_RAW_IN/HEALTH_SYNC_IN/HEALTH_QUAL_IN/HEALTH_ACTIVE/HEALTH_STICKY/RTL011_EVT_OVERFLOW_STATUS/HEALTH_QUALIFICATION/HEALTH_STATUS are all readback=external; HEALTH_CONTROL/HEALTH_POLARITY/HEALTH_FAULT_ENABLE/HEALTH_EVENT_ENABLE/HEALTH_IRQ_ENABLE/HEALTH_QUAL_0_3/HEALTH_QUAL_4_7 are all readback=internal_reg (plain RW, host read returns RTL-001's own stored value, not an RTL-011 echo -- no status_registers entry needed for these, same pattern as every other module's plain configuration RW registers).",
